P46,80471040,354347520,,,56262360,,,34804864,38898341,2026-11-05,2026-09-05,"MIXED CONFIGURATIONS -- DO NOT COMPARE THE TWO WINDOWS FIGURES WITH ANY OTHER ROW. linux_gtk4 is a release build and is comparable. windows_gtk4 and windows_winui are DEBUG builds and are roughly 43 percent larger than they would be at release: P0 windows_gtk4 is 56.5 MB at release against P46 debug at 80.5 MB, and nothing about P46 is 24 MB bigger than P0. The release builds were attempted and abandoned on cost: five consecutive ten-minute slices with zero errors got as far as Compiling Gtk Application.swift and did not link, because release recompiles SwiftSyntax, SwiftParser and Gtk with optimisation -- a fixed per-configuration cost that the debug tree had already paid. The same release build finished inside ONE call on WSL, which is the 20-100x Windows process-spawn cost recorded in task #58 showing up in a place that looks like a compiler problem. This is NOT the situation the Android column is in: that column is debug throughout and it does not matter, because release and debug measure 0.1 percent apart there (P12: 181824952 against 181629584) since the size is the statically linked runtime either way. On Windows the configuration dominates. Regenerate with SCUI_DEBUG=1 zsh compile.zsh -gtk4 P46 and SCUI_DEBUG=1 zsh compile.zsh P46 -- no BUILD_CONFIG, which is what makes them release -- then stat -c %s the two exes and replace both numbers and this note."
